# Settings of the dashboard build. Copy this file to `.env` (ignored by Git). Vite reads `VITE_` variables at BUILD time and writes
# them into the page, so they are public: never put a secret here (the dashboard needs none).

# Address of the API, only for a build that is served from a different address than the API (a static host). Leave it empty for
# `npm run dev` and `npm run preview`: the page then calls its own address and the Vite server forwards /api to the API.
# The API must list this page's address in its CORS_ORIGINS.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Not a .env setting: to make the dev server forward /api somewhere other than http://127.0.0.1:8000, set VITE_DEV_API_TARGET in the
# shell that starts it (vite.config.js reads the process environment), for example   VITE_DEV_API_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8001 npm run dev
